// expect: 7
// A parameter named like an effect op is the parameter where it is called.
// `result` below is `apply`'s own argument, and the judgment resolves the
// call to it; the lowering resolved the name against the module env instead
// and emitted a perform of the prelude's `Iterate` op `result`, which no
// handler serves here, so the program checked clean and aborted at run
// time. Found in the compiler's own source (src/derive.mn's `jvp_pair`,
// whose parameter `result` shadows the same op) on 2026-09-28, measured on
// boot 51f332d7.
fn apply(result, x: Int) -> Int = result(x)

fn main() -> Int = apply({ n => n + 2 }, 5)
